\\n\\n\\n](https://app.quicktype.io/)\\n\\n## Free AI Assistants\\n\\nAI tools to help you learn and code faster\\n\\n[Claude](https://claude.ai/)[Grok](https://grok.com/)[Gemini](https://gemini.google.com/)[ChatGPT](https://chatgpt.com/)\\n\\n## Code Like a Pro\\n\\nFree resources for learning different languages and technologies\\n\\n![Code Like a Pro - Free learning resources](/_next/image?url=%2Fimages%2Fresources%2Fcode-like-a-pro.png&w=828&q=75)\\n\\n[HTMLW3Schools.com](https://w3schools.com/)[CSSCodecademy.com](https://www.codecademy.com/learn/learn-css)[JavaScriptfreecodecamp.org](https://www.freecodecamp.org/learn/javascript-algorithms-and-data-structures/)[Reactreact.dev](https://react.dev/)[Pythonlearnpython.org](https://learnpython.org/)[Javasololearn.com](https://www.sololearn.com/)[PHPphp.net](https://www.php.net/manual/en/tutorial.php)[Cybersecuritytryhackme.com](https://tryhackme.com/)[Clearn-c.org](https://learn-c.org/)[C++learncpp.com](https://www.learncpp.com/)[AWSskillbuilder.aws](https://skillbuilder.aws/)[AI / MLcoursera.org](https://www.coursera.org/)[Gitlearngitbranching.js.org](https://learngitbranching.js.org/)[SQLsqlbolt.com](https://sqlbolt.com/)\\n\\n## Utilities\\n\\nHelpful tools and services\\n\\n[\\n\\nServerHunter\\n\\nFind cheap VPS and server deals\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.serverhunter.com/)[\\n\\nMAS Genuine ISO\\n\\nGenuine Windows installation media\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://massgrave.dev/genuine-installation-media)\\n\\n## Discord Text Formatting\\n\\nLearn how to format your messages in Discord\\n\\n![Discord text formatting guide](/images/resources/discord-text-formating.gif)\",\"description\":\"Curated learning resources, tools, and guides for developers\",\"url\":\"/resources\",\"category\":\"Resources\",\"locale\":\"en\"},\"9\":{\"title\":\"JavaScript & Full-Stack Development\",\"content\":\"# JavaScript & Full-Stack Development\\n\\n## Why JavaScript?\\n\\nJavaScript is the easiest path to becoming a full-stack developer. With a single language, you can build everything from interactive websites to server-side applications, mobile apps, and even desktop software.\\n\\n## Web Dev Speedrun\\n\\nThis is the exact path I took to learn web development. Follow these resources in order to build a good foundation in HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. Each resource builds on the previous one.\\n\\n[\\n\\n1Responsive Web Design\\n\\nFreeCodeCamp - HTML & CSS fundamentals\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.freecodecamp.org/learn/responsive-web-design/)[\\n\\n2Learn HTML\\n\\nCodecademy - Deep dive into HTML\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.codecademy.com/learn/learn-html)[\\n\\n3Learn CSS\\n\\nCodecademy - Master CSS styling\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.codecademy.com/learn/learn-css)[\\n\\n4Responsive Web Design (2022)\\n\\nFreeCodeCamp - Updated HTML & CSS curriculum\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.freecodecamp.org/learn/2022/responsive-web-design/)[\\n\\n5JavaScript Algorithms & Data Structures\\n\\nFreeCodeCamp - Core JavaScript concepts\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.freecodecamp.org/learn/javascript-algorithms-and-data-structures/)[\\n\\n6Introduction to JavaScript\\n\\nCodecademy - JavaScript fundamentals\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.codecademy.com/learn/introduction-to-javascript)[\\n\\n7JavaScript Algorithms & Data Structures (v8)\\n\\nFreeCodeCamp - Latest JavaScript curriculum\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.freecodecamp.org/learn/javascript-algorithms-and-data-structures-v8/)\\n\\n## Node.js\\n\\nNode.js lets you run JavaScript on the server, making you a true full-stack developer. With Node.js, you can build APIs, handle databases, and create complete web applications using the same language you learned for the frontend. Download it from [nodejs.org](https://nodejs.org/en/download).\\n\\n## React\\n\\nOnce you've learned the basics and Node.js, it's time to master React. React is the most popular JavaScript library for building user interfaces and is used by companies like Meta, Netflix, and Airbnb.\\n\\n[\\n\\nReact Official Docs\\n\\nThe best place to learn React from scratch\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://react.dev/learn)[\\n\\nReact Tutorial for Beginners\\n\\nFreeCodeCamp - Comprehensive React course\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.freecodecamp.org/news/learn-react-course/)\\n\\n## Designing with shadcn/ui\\n\\n[shadcn/ui](https://ui.shadcn.com/) is a collection of beautifully designed, accessible components that you can copy and paste into your apps. It's built on top of Radix UI and Tailwind CSS, giving you full control over your components.\\n\\n### Component Libraries & Blocks\\n\\nThese libraries provide pre-built components and blocks that work seamlessly with shadcn/ui.\\n\\n[\\n\\nAwesome shadcn\\n\\nCurated list of shadcn resources\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.shadcn.io/awesome)[\\n\\nOrigin UI\\n\\nBeautiful UI components\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://originui.com/)[\\n\\nAnimate UI\\n\\nAnimated components for React\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://animate-ui.com/)[\\n\\nMVP Blocks\\n\\nReady-to-use blocks for MVPs\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://blocks.mvp-subha.me/)[\\n\\nSHSF UI\\n\\nModern component library\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.shsfui.com/)[\\n\\nKibo UI\\n\\nAccessible component library\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.kibo-ui.com/)[\\n\\nReact Bits\\n\\nUseful React components\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://reactbits.dev/)[\\n\\nSkiper UI\\n\\nUI components collection\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://skiper-ui.com/)[\\n\\nAceternity UI\\n\\nBeautiful animated components\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://ui.aceternity.com/)[\\n\\nMagic UI\\n\\nMagical UI components\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://magicui.design/)[\\n\\nCult UI\\n\\nModern design system\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://cult-ui.com/)\\n\\n### Tools & Utilities\\n\\nHelpful tools for customizing and extending shadcn/ui.\\n\\n[\\n\\nTweakCN\\n\\nCustomize shadcn themes visually\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://tweakcn.com/)[\\n\\nAwesome shadcn/ui\\n\\nGitHub collection of shadcn resources\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://github.com/birobirobiro/awesome-shadcn-ui)\",\"description\":\"JavaScript is the easiest path to becoming a full-stack developer. With a single language, you can build everything from interactive websites to server-side applications, mobile apps, and even desktop...\",\"url\":\"/resources/languages/javascript\",\"category\":\"Resources\",\"locale\":\"en\"},\"10\":{\"title\":\"Python\",\"content\":\"# Python\\n\\nPython is really only relevant for specific fields like data science, machine learning, scientific computing, and automation scripting. Outside of these areas, it's not particularly useful.\\n\\nMany people choose Python as their first language because they think it's simple. While the syntax is readable, this simplicity doesn't transfer well to other languages or real-world development. If you want to become a full-stack developer, JavaScript is a much better choice since it works on both frontend and backend.\\n\\nBut if you really want to learn Python, check out [FreeCodeCamp's Scientific Computing with Python](https://www.freecodecamp.org/learn/scientific-computing-with-python/) or [Codecademy's Python courses](https://www.codecademy.com/catalog/language/python).\",\"description\":\"Python is really only relevant for specific fields like data science, machine learning, scientific computing, and automation scripting. Outside of these areas, it's not particularly useful.\",\"url\":\"/resources/languages/python\",\"category\":\"Resources\",\"locale\":\"en\"},\"11\":{\"title\":\"Vibe Coding\",\"content\":\"# Vibe Coding\\n\\n## What is Vibe Coding?\\n\\nVibe coding is a new approach to programming where you describe what you want in natural language and let AI build it for you. Instead of writing every line of code yourself, you guide the AI with prompts and let it handle the implementation.\\n\\nThe term was coined by Andrej Karpathy in this tweet:\\n\\nTo vibe code effectively, you need the right tools. Here are the best AI-powered editors and CLIs available today.\\n\\n## Choosing the Best Model\\n\\nThe AI model you use matters just as much as the tool. You can find the latest rankings of AI models for web development on the [LM Arena Web Development Leaderboard](https://lmarena.ai/leaderboard/webdev).\\n\\nThat said, Claude models by Anthropic consistently rank at the top for coding tasks. If you want the best results for vibe coding, Claude is usually the way to go.\\n\\n## My Setup\\n\\nI personally use the [Claude Code VSCode Extension](https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=anthropics.claude-code) for my vibe coding workflow. It integrates Claude directly into VSCode with agentic capabilities.\\n\\nTo help gather context for AI assistants, I also built the [Code Collector](https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=0-don.code-collector) extension. It automatically collects files based on import dependencies, making it easy to provide your codebase context to any AI assistant.\\n\\n## AI Editors\\n\\nThese editors have AI deeply integrated into the coding experience, allowing you to chat with AI, generate code, and get intelligent completions.\\n\\n[\\n\\nCursor\\n\\nAI-first code editor built on VSCode\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://cursor.com/)[\\n\\nWindsurf\\n\\nAI-powered IDE by Codeium\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://codeium.com/windsurf)[\\n\\nAntigravity\\n\\nAI coding environment\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://antigravity.google/)\\n\\n## AI CLIs\\n\\nCommand-line tools that let you vibe code directly from your terminal. These are great for quick tasks, automation, and working in any editor you prefer.\\n\\n[\\n\\nClaude Code\\n\\nAnthropic's agentic coding CLI\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code)[\\n\\nOpenAI Codex CLI\\n\\nOpenAI's terminal coding assistant\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://github.com/openai/codex)[\\n\\nGemini CLI\\n\\nGoogle's AI coding assistant for terminal\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://github.com/google-gemini/gemini-cli)\",\"description\":\"Vibe coding is a new approach to programming where you describe what you want in natural language and let AI build it for you. Instead of writing every line of code yourself, you guide the AI with pro...\",\"url\":\"/resources/guides/vibe-coding\",\"category\":\"Resources\",\"locale\":\"en\"},\"12\":{\"title\":\"Cyber Security\",\"content\":\"# Cyber Security\\n\\n## Introduction\\n\\nLet's be honest - most of us got into cyber security because we wanted to be hackers. We imagined ourselves breaking into systems, bypassing firewalls, and doing cool stuff like in the movies. Then reality hit: turns out hacking is mostly just... coding. A lot of coding.\\n\\nBut that's actually the good news. The skills you learn in cyber security - understanding systems, networks, and how software works - make you a better developer overall. Whether you end up in pentesting, security engineering, or just writing more secure code, it all starts with the fundamentals.\\n\\n## Learning Platforms\\n\\nThe best way to learn cyber security is by doing. These platforms offer hands-on challenges, CTFs, and virtual labs where you can practice legally and safely.\\n\\n[\\n\\nTryHackMe\\n\\nFree online platform for learning cyber security with hands-on exercises and labs\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://tryhackme.com/)[\\n\\nHack The Box\\n\\nCyber mastery platform with beginner-friendly modules and real-world challenges\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://hackthebox.com/)[\\n\\npicoCTF\\n\\nFree computer security education program by Carnegie Mellon University\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.picoctf.org/)[\\n\\nRoot Me\\n\\nPlatform for practicing hacking skills with challenges and virtual environments\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://www.root-me.org/)[\\n\\nCisco Networking Academy\\n\\nLearn cybersecurity, networking, and Python from Cisco's official training program\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](https://netacad.com/)\",\"description\":\"Let's be honest - most of us got into cyber security because we wanted to be hackers. We imagined ourselves breaking into systems, bypassing firewalls, and doing cool stuff like in the movies. Then re...\",\"url\":\"/resources/guides/cyber-security\",\"category\":\"Resources\",\"locale\":\"en\"},\"13\":{\"title\":\"JavaScript\",\"content\":\"# JavaScript(110)\\n\\n[\\n\\n### Here are my portfolios codes, please check them well\\n\\nhttps://github.com/bekamanjgaladze3-dev This is my github profile links where all of my works are there and can you tell me wheather i am ready for front end jubior developer jobs? For upwork and companies seperately?\\n\\nB\\n\\nBarrie\\n\\nVerified\\n\\n2 messages\\n\\n2 members\\n\\n8 hours ago\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](/en/community/coding/javascript/1458034492831825975)\\n\\n[\\n\\n### /ban command for my Discord bot\\n\\nI'm trying to make my own /ban command for my Discord bot, I would like to recreate the official Discord command with the same wide choice of options to delete messages (All the messages from 1 hour ago, 3 hours ago, 6 hours ago...) but I can't figure out how to do it\\n\\nN\\n\\n๖̶ζ͜͡?᲼᲼᲼𝓝𝓪𝓪𝓼𝓴𝓪𝓻\\n\\nCopy Paster!\\n\\n3 messages\\n\\n3 members\\n\\n11 days ago\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](/en/community/coding/javascript/1454275863427420191)\\n\\n[\\n\\n### Broken index.js\\n\\nN\\n\\n๖̶ζ͜͡?᲼᲼᲼𝓝𝓪𝓪𝓼𝓴𝓪𝓻\\n\\nCopy Paster!\\n\\n1 messages\\n\\n1 members\\n\\n21 days ago\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](/en/community/coding/javascript/1450595030225129522)\\n\\n[\\n\\n### Discord Slash commands Moderation Type help discord@13\\n\\nI currently need help creating commands of a modbots I have completely no idea how to make moderation commands I have other commands in index.js \\\\*\\\\*Problem:\\\\*\\\\* I Can Code Many commands in index.js but I need help creating mod commands \\\\*\\\\*What do I use?\\\\*\\\\* I currently use visual studio code and node.js So anyone who knows kinda help me.\\n\\nZ\\n\\nℨ𝔬𝔥𝔞𝔫𝖃\\n\\nPlaying Custom Status\\n\\nVerified\\n\\n2 messages\\n\\n2 members\\n\\n21 days ago\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n]