guage\\n\\ngo\\n\\n🚀 ArachnoScript — a JavaScript-inspired programming language by ECMA King (me) - Object-oriented & functional features - Includes a web-focused standard library (Verdex + ASX) - Binaries for Linux, Mac, Windows (no source exposed) License: Non-commercial — free for learning, experimentation, and personal projects GitHub: https://github.com/ECMA-King87/ArachnoScript-Programming-Language.git Examples in the README\\n\\nE\\n\\nECMA King 👑\\n\\nVerified\\n\\n10 Nachrichten\\n\\n3 Mitglieder\\n\\n3 days ago\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](/de/community/showcase/1457051946836824167)\\n\\n[\\n\\n![MusicDom: a Streamlit Music Player](/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcdn.discordapp.com%2Fattachments%2F1456828053773881397%2F1456828054415347732%2FMusicDom_Logo.jpeg%3Fex%3D695e659a%26is%3D695d141a%26hm%3De58d8f043f7869ee442ba7d4830fda1f3d0a473c625863311f0ecf56736ca1eb%26&w=3840&q=75)\\n\\n### MusicDom: a Streamlit Music Player\\n\\npython\\n\\nSo, I was kind of pissed with current Music Streaming services recently and, thus, decided to build my own. It is a very simple, streamlit app yet in the beginning. It currently supports simple music playing by accessing your local music folder, Music downloader and metadata modification. The app uses the metadata of the songs to automatically provide a cover when playing the song. it still has a long way to go and a lot of basic functions to add, but things are flowing smoothly :) You can check it out here: https://github.com/oRiquelmy/MusicDom Suggestions and constructive criticism would be greatly appreciated!\\n\\nO\\n\\nᗩᗷIGᗩIᒪ\\n\\nVerified\\n\\n1 Nachrichten\\n\\n1 Mitglieder\\n\\n4 days ago\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](/de/community/showcase/1456828053773881397)\\n\\n[\\n\\n### Looking for Discord Bot Developer\\n\\nHi! I’m looking for a developer who can make a Discord bot for Fortnite scrims (queue, custom games, etc.). DM me if you’re interested ASAP.\\n\\nP\\n\\npepuu\\n\\nSpielt Fortnite\\n\\nVerified\\n\\n4 Nachrichten