ly manage hundreds of notes, organize them into folders, export them, and boost your productivity with custom snippets, markdown shortcuts, and more. ## 🛠 Tech stack: - Frontend: Vue.js + Nuxt - Backend: Go - Storage: MinIO + MySQL I’m currently the only developer working on it, but I’d love to have contributors! Whether you’re into coding, UI/UX, documentation, or just want to share feedback and suggestions, you're very welcome to join 🫶 👉 GitHub repo: https://github.com/Smaug6739/Alexandrie If you like the idea, a ⭐ on GitHub would mean a lot — and feel free to reach out if you want to get involved!\\n\\nS\\n\\nExpress.js\\n\\n0 Nachrichten\\n\\n0 Mitglieder\\n\\n5 months ago\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](/de/community/showcase/1406346077136879627)\\n\\n[\\n\\n![My first red team project. Have mercy](/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcdn.discordapp.com%2Fattachments%2F1406123852937039995%2F1406123853343621231%2FIMG_8059.png%3Fex%3D695e81a3%26is%3D695d3023%26hm%3De8853af1be6e8a14602370eb8469266eee975e24da4ca206d743a818049ebd0a%26&w=3840&q=75)\\n\\n### My first red team project. Have mercy\\n\\nArchiviert 4 months ago\\n\\nI built a CRT-less manual map loader that’s only 4KB, handling relocations, imports, API hashing, syscall fallbacks, and stealth memory protections without relying on the C runtime. The loader carries an encrypted, embedded stage2 that’s 11KB and also CRT-less, it installs a root CA, sets the system proxy to an external server, and adds stealth layers like AMSI and ETW patching, NTDLL unhooking, and UAC elevation. Small footprint, no CRT overhead, fully obfuscated, and tuned for quiet execution. Each payload build is polymorphic due to encryption and section renaming.\\n\\nN\\n\\nVibe Coder!\\n\\n4 Nachrichten\\n\\n1 Mitglieder\\n\\n5 months ago\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](/de/community/showcase/1406123852937039995)\\n\\n[\\n\\n![🎨 SubSlay.app – Turn your text into color!](/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcdn.discordapp.com%2Fattachments%2F1405938354985373747%2F1405938355287359562%2Fi_love_tree.png%3Fex%3D695e7da0%26is%3D695d2c20%26hm%3D1b83ff0c894f778f0976deb7172062b7224dcfd1b682d72c84f554be1405ac75%26&w=3840&q=75)\\n\\n### 🎨 SubSlay.app – Turn your text into color!\\n\\nArchiviert 4 months ago\\n\\nrust\\n\\nType anything, and every word gets its own unique hue. Make your messages pop, express vibes, or just have fun with colors — all instantly! 🌈\\n\\nA\\n\\nandria\\n\\nVerified\\n\\n7 Nachrichten\\n\\n2 Mitglieder\\n\\n5 months ago\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](/de/community/showcase/1405938354985373747)\\n\\n[\\n\\n### Cybersecurity tool\\n\\nArchiviert 4 months ago\\n\\npython\\n\\nQuick cybersecurity tool for pentesting called Netra. terminal based tool pure py works on linux environments. It is a red team tool for network scanning spectically via mDNS. Feel free to dm for script\\n\\nJ\\n\\nJonas Savimbe\\n\\nScript Kiddie!\\n\\n1 Nachrichten\\n\\n2 Mitglieder\\n\\n5 months ago\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](/de/community/showcase/1405764488170311852)\\n\\n[\\n\\n### Conquer server emulation\\n\\nArchiviert 4 months ago\\n\\nc#\\n\\nhttps://github.com/berniemackie97/OpenConquerPub Making an open source server emulation for an old game I used to play as a kid. It's been a fun experience reverse engineering the client to figure out the packet structures and communication encryptions. If anyone is interested in joining up or expanding on it it's fully open source. This has been pretty fun so far so if you have any other ideas or games you'd like to start a project doing this one I'd be more than happy to join!\\n\\nB\\n\\nCopy Paster!\\n\\n0 Nachrichten\\n\\n0 Mitglieder\\n\\n5 months ago\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](/de/community/showcase/1405407656033652736)\\n\\n[\\n\\n### Guest blog service\\n\\nArchiviert 4 months ago\\n\\nR\\n\\nRamsey John\\n\\nVerified\\n\\n0 Nachrichten\\n\\n1 Mitglieder\\n\\n5 months ago\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](/de/community/showcase/1404997245044260904)\\n\\n[\\n\\n### Agentika File: Optimization Files using Artificial intelligence (AI)\\n\\nArchiviert 4 months ago\\n\\nHey everyone, I'd like to share a project I've been working on. ### \\\\*\\\\*Project Details\\\\*\\\\* \\\\* \\\\*\\\\*Project Name:\\\\*\\\\* Agentika File 🤖 \\\\* \\\\*\\\\*Brief Description:\\\\*\\\\* Agentika File is a smart web app that uses AI to automatically compress your files. Instead of just applying one setting, it acts as an intelligent agent that tries multiple strategies in a sequence until it successfully makes the file smaller. The entire process is transparent and happens privately in your browser. ### \\\\*\\\\*Tech Stack\\\\*\\\\* \\\\* \\\\*\\\\*Frontend:\\\\*\\\\* React, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS \\\\* \\\\*\\\\*AI Engine:\\\\*\\\\* Google Gemini 2.5-Flash with Structured Output \\\\* \\\\*\\\\*Compression:\\\\*\\\\* The \\\\`browser-image-compression\\\\` library \\\\* \\\\*\\\\*Core Architecture:\\\\*\\\\* Iterative Reduction Cascade (IRC) ### \\\\*\\\\*Key Features & Challenges Overcome\\\\*\\\\* The main goal was to solve the common frustration of \\\"file too large\\\" errors and the tedious trial-and-error of manual compression. \\\\* \\\\*\\\\*Iterative Reduction Cascade (IRC):\\\\*\\\\* This is the core feature. The AI designs a \\\"ladder\\\" of compression strategies, from gentle to aggressive. If one attempt fails to reduce the file size, it automatically tries the next one. It doesn't give up. \\\\* \\\\*\\\\*100% Browser-Side Privacy:\\\\*\\\\* No files are ever uploaded to a server. All the processing is done directly in your browser, which means your data is completely private and the process is very fast. \\\\* \\\\*\\\\*Radical Transparency:\\\\*\\\\* You can watch the AI \\\"struggle\\\" in a live log. It shows you every attempt, failure, and which strategy finally succeeded. I'd love to hear your thoughts and any feedback you might have. Let me know what you think\\n\\nA\\n\\nArdelyo\\n\\nVerified\\n\\n2 Nachrichten\\n\\n3 Mitglieder\\n\\n5 months ago\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](/de/community/showcase/1404787086552207452)\\n\\n[\\n\\n![QuickBrowse](/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcdn.discordapp.com%2Fattachments%2F1404775268358422600%2F1404775269851467847%2Fimage.png%3Fex%3D695e36eb%26is%3D695ce56b%26hm%3Df240a051e5f8c67d2183569f98345a0a8f69d6af4a7e12b5df30ecf52f312dd7%26&w=3840&q=75)\\n\\n### QuickBrowse\\n\\nArchiviert 3 months ago\\n\\nQuickBrowse is a Browse especially designed for browsing together, with QuickBrowse you can create browsing sessions with friends, where you have a Chat for communicating, you can watch together Youtube videos with real time sync aswell as tab and url sync, you see where your friend is and you can even share your cursor to show him something.Another feature is SplitView you can view multiple Tabs at once to improve productivity. But its not fully done, im currently working on the UI and improving performance. For more information look on my Github or DM me github: https://github.com/KreakxX/QuickBrowse feel free to star my Repo 👍\\n\\nK\\n\\nKreakxX\\n\\nHelper\\n\\n46 Nachrichten\\n\\n5 Mitglieder\\n\\n5 months ago\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](/de/community/showcase/1404775268358422600)\\n\\n[\\n\\n### shadcn-cookies\\n\\nArchiviert 4 months ago\\n\\nhtml & css\\n\\nSleek and flexible cookie consent component, designed with shadcn/ui site: https://shadcn-cookies.vercel.app gh: https://github.com/kaizenics/shadcn-cookies\\n\\nN\\n\\nNiko\\n\\nVerified\\n\\n0 Nachrichten\\n\\n1 Mitglieder\\n\\n5 months ago\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](/de/community/showcase/1404526270632693972)\\n\\n[\\n\\n![iOS app Feedbacks (Learning App)](/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcdn.discordapp.com%2Fattachments%2F1403911993823596564%2F1403911994209337436%2Fview_1.png%3Fex%3D695e5eae%26is%3D695d0d2e%26hm%3D10f213182253162807f13c0067b91337eef46302393c89613fc83a19171d50f7%26&w=3840&q=75)\\n\\n### iOS app Feedbacks (Learning App)\\n\\nArchiviert 2 months ago\\n\\npython\\n\\nHey everyone! My brother and I just launched a small Duolingo-style app for learning Python — gamified, short levels and fun animations. We’re just starting out and would really love honest feedback—what’s confusing, what’s fun, what’s broken. 👉 Try it: https://apps.apple.com/us/app/sideme-learn-coding/id6743945588 If you’ve got 2 minutes, drop thoughts here—screenshots/bugs super welcome!\\n\\nJ\\n\\nJason\\n\\nVerified\\n\\n8 Nachrichten\\n\\n6 Mitglieder\\n\\n5 months ago\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](/de/community/showcase/1403911993823596564)\\n\\n[\\n\\n### Medium Post :Monitoring Spring Boot Code Quality with SonarQube on Docker and Kubernetes\\n\\nArchiviert 4 months ago\\n\\nCode Quality Monitoring for Spring Boot: SonarQube on Docker & Kubernetes In this hands-on guide, you’ll learn how to: 🔹 Integrate SonarQube for static code analysis in your Spring Boot app 🔸 Run local analysis via Docker Compose for instant feedback 🔹 Deploy SonarQube on Kubernetes with persistent storage 🔸 Track bugs, vulnerabilities, code smells, and technical debt trends over time For more details, check out the Medium link below — this article covers everything you need to know. Link ▶️ https://medium.com/@sngermiyanoglu/monitoring-spring-boot-code-quality-with-sonarqube-on-docker-and-kubernetes-e7b9f6feb75c\\n\\nD\\n\\ndirect\\\\_x\\\\_34\\n\\nCopy Paster!\\n\\n0 Nachrichten\\n\\n1 Mitglieder\\n\\n5 months ago\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](/de/community/showcase/1403864146797138021)\\n\\n[\\n\\n### Hack United\\n\\nArchiviert 4 months ago\\n\\nIf you’re a student serious about STEM or entrepreneurship, this is the opportunity you’ve been looking for. Registrations are now open for \\\\[\\\\*\\\\*United Hacks V6\\\\*\\\\*\\\\](https://www.hackunited.org/) — one of the most prestigious virtual hackathons worldwide. > 📍 100% virtual & completely free > 📅 January 16 - 18, 2026 > 🧠 Open to all experience levels (high school, university, etc) > 💰 \\\\*\\\\*$50,000+ in prizes\\\\*\\\\*, mentorship from industry leaders > 🔥 Previous judges from \